+From: PonWrt developers <noreply@localhost>
+Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: classify WED IRQs and drain stalled forwarding
+
+Counting irq_set_mask(0) counted both the mt7915 hard IRQ and tasklet,
+and could disable the WED line while DMA still made progress. Count
+serviced WED causes once, ignore native-only service, and sample DMA
+progress before classifying high-rate normal events as stalled.
+Track high-rate hardware errors separately so moving traffic cannot
+hide a persistent error flood.
+
+Quarantine a confirmed fault through work that closes the PPE egress
+gate, invalidates flows and drains DMA. Serialize that drain with
+consumer teardown and retain uncertain DMA ownership. Stop paths must
+still drain after quarantine, and diagnostics must expose the IRQ state.
+
+Signed-off-by: PonWrt developers <noreply@localhost>
+---
+diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_wed.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_wed.c
+--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_wed.c
++++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_wed.c
